# What dbt's sdist needs in order to build, pinned and hashed like everything
# it builds (pipeline/ELT.md decision 144). requirements-dbt.txt's hashes
# cover dbt's sdist and every wheel, and they do not reach this: the 2.0.6
# sdist's pyproject.toml declares `requires = ["packaging>=24"]` for its build
# backend, and pip installs a build's requirements into a throwaway
# environment from PyPI, at the newest version the range allows, with no hash
# even under --require-hashes (measured 2026-10-10 on pip 24.0: "Collecting
# packaging>=24 ... Successfully installed packaging-26.3"). The backend
# imports it before it fetches and checks dbt's wheel, so it is code that runs
# inside the check.
#
# So every install puts this file in first, hash-checked, and then installs
# requirements-dbt.txt with --no-build-isolation, which builds dbt with what
# is already installed and fetches nothing for the build. Without this file
# in first, that build stops with "No module named 'packaging'" rather than
# fetching it (measured the same day). pip 25.3 and later have
# --build-constraint, which hash-checks a build's requirements too (measured
# on pip 26.2.1), but the venvs CI makes carry pip 25.0.1 (run 38001863592).
#
# Read the build requirements again from dbt's sdist when the dbt pin moves.
# Compile from pipeline/ on Python 3.12:
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements-dbt-build.txt --strip-extras requirements-dbt-build.in
packaging>=24
